  "title": "Oikonomou2016 – SSVEP MAMEM 1 dataset",
  "description": "A dataset of 256-channel EEG recordings from 11 healthy adults performing an SSVEP-based BCI protocol. Participants viewed a single flickering magenta box at five stimulation frequencies (6.66, 7.50, 8.57, 10.00 and 12.00 Hz) while EEG was recorded at 250 Hz. The data support comparative evaluation of state-of-the-art SSVEP signal-processing and classification algorithms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with an EGI 300 Geodesic EEG System and a 256-channel HydroCel Geodesic Sensor Net at 250 Hz. Each session consisted of 100 s of rest, an adaptation period of eight 5 s flicker windows, and then three 5 s flicker windows for each of the five frequencies in ascending order, separated by rest periods. The stimulus was a flickering box shown on a 60 Hz LCD monitor.",
